            "data": "id\tsource\ttitle\twhen\tchunk_number\tcontent\tdense\tgtp_timestamp\n1869447301\thttps://blendata.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BE1/pages/1869447301/JSON+File\tJSON File\t2023-11-15T07:04:18.418Z\t0\tJavaScript Object Notation(JSON) is a text format, which typically contains data organized in key-value pairs and arrays, where keys are strings and values can be strings, numbers, booleans, null, objects, or other nested JSON structures. Here\u0027s a simple example: json \"name\" , \"age\" , \"occupation\" , and \"city\" are Key . \"Smith Lee\" , 30 , \"Teacher\" , \"Bangkok\" are Value . \"language\" is a key with an array as its value. Input File Setting: Multiline options : To separate the values in the same line and create the new line.\tWrappedArray(-0.026981553, 0.04446096, -0.007253272, 0.018233044, -0.07136358, -0.005594205, 0.023277592, 0.03724153, 0.023807697, -0.03195429, 0.0049852384, 0.065307334, -0.014695199, 0.021422852, 0.06122253, 0.07032912, -0.15932651, -0.0068191513, -0.077436484, -0.08718371, 0.0889905, -0.018244518, -0.07614426, -0.019120434, 0.010633965, 0.10268885, 0.08722995, 0.01696773, -0.048862457, 0.07796076, -0.03761721, -0.07065527, 0.09044783, 0.040462945, -0.0259771, 0.02853446, 0.004286901, -0.02624843, 0.017971164, 0.025158972, -0.011362164, 0.026704108, -0.04176032, -0.07216718, 0.060452234, -9.544211E-5, -0.069291696, -0.052816793, -0.025171207, 0.091801256, -0.017516643, 0.038535815, -0.07397068, 0.02735323, 2.773368E-4, -0.004193796, -0.06567498, 0.004682088, -0.013016378, -0.011334329, -0.023465505, 0.06639918, 0.037078414, 0.07337124, 0.083077855, -0.049203247, -0.05665982, 0.058601137, 3.525606E-4, -0.016264819, 0.00957686, 0.011739067, 0.027965989, -0.031736333, 0.0026758418, -0.0788219, -0.037959773, 0.014242195, 0.045637555, 0.08466628, -0.0020004066, -0.030355476, -0.049090054, 0.052628227, -0.03996233, 0.039617404, -0.0050769686, -0.020599518, 0.009764745, 0.03161416, -0.097820126, -0.06823057, 0.0502251